<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22663" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incursĭo</span></b> , ōnis,
			f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				running against</i>, <i>onset</i>, <i>assault</i>, <i>attack</i> (class.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">atomorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 1, 41, 114</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">atque impetus armatorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Caecin. 15, 44</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Quint. 6, 4, 14</span></i> Spald. <i>N. cr.</i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In partic., <i>a hostile inroad</i>, <i>incursion</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hostiliter in fines Romanos incursionem facit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					1, 11, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prohibere hostem ab incursionibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. G. 6, 10 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subitas hostium incursiones sustinere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hirt. B. G. 8, 11 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">moliri incursionem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					6, 28, 32, § 146</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
